#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 136 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object parses a time string in the form "HH:MM:SS[.XXX]"
and outputs the corresponding value in seconds as a float. Hours and
minutes may be omitted \, so short forms like "M:SS" or even "S" (just
a number) are also accepted. This is the inverse operation of [conv.sec2str].
If the input string cannot be parsed \, the value of the @on_err property
is output instead.;
